  "after": null,
  "findings": [
    "Artifact per-request cost is dominated by Registry owner HTTP wait: 0.261425s socket receive out of 0.269926s total for 329 rows; normalizing 329 rows takes 0.003405s cumulative. Concurrent BFF reads alone cannot remove the owner population cost.",
    "Strategies bounded owner page takes 0.539459s in the separate owner-port profile (166 non-draft rows), including 0.537118s in http_request_json; nine-read hosted strategies p95 is 3.231841s. This does not isolate the complete strategies route or prove all remaining cost is in the BFF.",
    "ResearchRouterService.list_artifact_catalog calls both complete-list owner ports on each request, concatenates and sorts all rows, then slices with numeric offsets.",
    "Registry GET /api/registry/strategy-artifacts accepts page tokens but its service first builds all visible rows; PostgresRegistryStore.list_strategy_artifact_rows uses list_all_selected without a page bound.",
    "Research GET /api/research/artifacts returns an unpaged list from _visible_saved_artifacts, which scans runs/artifacts and sorts all visible rows.",
    "To satisfy constant per-page work, the owner contracts need an indexed ordered catalog read (including exact totals and deterministic cross-owner merge boundaries) before the BFF can consume bounded pages. Merely reducing normalization, adding fan-out, or memoizing a complete BFF catalog does not establish this criterion."
  ],
